{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvamnsAsYsERQ9uzspUn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommendation: neither start nor drop yet. Spend a week or two on a cheap analysis, then decide.**\n\nThe evidence so far is thin but not trivial. Three requests and one lost deal in a month is a real signal. It's also an anecdote, and it comes from \"enterprise\" prospects who may not be your core segment. Because the data to settle this already exists, deciding now would be guessing.\n\n**Do this first (a few days, not months):**\n1. Re-read the 140 lost-deal records, including free-text notes and the sales reps' own recollection. Count deals where security, compliance or SOC 2 was a stated or likely factor. Loss-reason fields often hide this under \"other\" or \"no decision\".\n2. Pull the open pipeline and tag deals that have asked for SOC 2 or a security questionnaire, with their values.\n3. Compare the total annual contract value (ACV) at risk with the cost. £60k is probably recurring, since audits renew yearly, so count the ongoing cost too.\n\n**Suggested decision rule (adjust to your margins):** if SOC 2 plausibly cost or blocked deals worth more than about 2–3× the first-year cost, start now. If it's a handful of small deals, drop it. If it falls in between, go ahead only if you're moving upmarket.\n\n**Meanwhile, low-regret steps:**\n- Publish a security overview and answer questionnaires well.\n- Get a penetration test.\n- Write up your core policies.\n\nThese help win deals either way and cut the audit work later.\n\nI'd also ask whether a SOC 2 Type 1 report is faster and enough for most buyers. Many accept it as a first step.\n\nMy lean is that SOC 2 is likely worth doing for an HR tool, since it holds sensitive employee data. But the analysis should confirm that before you commit £60k."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3447,"cache_read_input_tokens":5036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3447},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad7e3795-040b-4d98-b067-1c0c7c9842e5","uuid":"94bcbd57-4903-4563-8178-f2c948a90ad1","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:09:57.929Z","request_id":"req_011Cfvamnc3PKgY7YiMRN9ia"}
